==English==

===Pronunciation===
*:Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ʌntʃ|-ʌntʃ]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}
#A [[stoop]]ed or [[curl]]ed [[posture]]; a [[slouch]].
#:''The old man walked with a '''hunch'''.''
#A [[theory]], [[idea]], or [[guess]].
#:''I have a '''hunch''' they'll find a way to solve the problem.''

====Translations====
*Portuguese: [[palpite]] {{m}}
*Spanish: [[corazonada]] {{f}} (2)

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}
#{{intransitive}} To slouch, stoop, curl, or lean.
#:''Do not '''hunch''' over your computer if you want to avoid neck problems.''

